# 🧠 Quizzler

A desktop True/False trivia quiz app built with Python and Tkinter, pulling live questions from the Open Trivia Database API.

---

## ✨ What It Does

Quizzler throws a series of True/False trivia questions at you, one at a time, in a clean GUI. Answer using the ✅ or ❌ buttons, get instant feedback, and watch your score update as you go.

## 🛠️ Built With

- **Python** — core logic
- **Tkinter** — GUI framework
- **Open Trivia DB API** — live trivia questions via `requests`

## 🎮 How It Works

1. On launch, the app fetches 10 random True/False questions from the Open Trivia DB.
2. Each question appears on a card-style canvas in the center of the window.
3. Click ✅ (True) or ❌ (False) to answer.
4. Instant feedback ("Correct!" / "Oops!") flashes briefly before the next question loads.
5. Your score updates live at the top of the screen.
6. Once all questions are answered, the app lets you know the quiz is complete.

## 🚀 Getting Started

**Requirements:**
```
pip install requests
```

**Run it:**
```
python main.py
```

Make sure the `images/` folder (containing `true.png` and `false.png`) is in the same directory as your project files.

## 📂 Project Structure

```
quizzler-app/
├── main.py           # Entry point — fetches questions, builds the quiz
├── quiz_brain.py      # Quiz logic — tracks score, checks answers
├── question_model.py  # Question data structure
├── ui.py              # Tkinter GUI
└── images/
    ├── true.png
    └── false.png
```

## 📌 Notes

Trivia questions and answers come from the [Open Trivia Database](https://opentdb.com/), so content updates each time you run the app.

